! C22-6578 PROBLEM 4.3, "BIT IMAGE OF A SEQUENCE OF NUMBERS", printed
! p.37 (PDF 38), Method 1, read in the ink at 300 dpi.
!
!   "Given 64 numbers in successive full words beginning at NUMB.  Many
!   of these are floating-point zeros, but some are not.  Create a full
!   word beginning at BIMAGE in which successive bits reflect the
!   condition of the successive words, such that a zero number will be
!   represented by a zero bit image and a nonzero will have a 1 bit as
!   image."  Comment (a): the image serves sparse matrix multiplication,
!   "tested via the logical connective 'and,' and the subsequent
!   querying of $AOC and $LZC" -- Problem 4.5.
!
! THE THIRTEEN PRINTED STATEMENTS FROM "LX, $1, XW1" TO "XW2 XW, BIMAGE, 0,
! $" ARE AS PRINTED, assembled by the host STRAP II (ASM=strap2).  The
! deck adds START on the first line, for END, and the data between two
! guards.  BIMAGE starts as all ones, so "Z, BIMAGE" is seen.  Reading:
! "(V+I)" is printed with the I's serif touching the parenthesis; it is
! (V+I), as the assembled word shows.  A speck after XW2's "$" is a mark
! in the paper.
!
! WHAT THE PROGRAM DOES, by the Reference Manual (22-6530-2, printed
! page = PDF - 3):
!   Z, BIMAGE          STORE ZERO (p.31).
!   LU  L(U), NUMB($1) a floating LOAD, unnormalized; it sets the
!                      arithmetic result indicators "as in ADD" (p.88),
!                      and "the indicator RZ is turned on for all zero
!                      result fractions" (p.85): A ZERO HERE IS A ZERO
!                      FRACTION, whatever the exponent, sign or flags.
!   BZRZ, FIX          non-zero: CM1111(BU,1)(V+I),0.1($2), CONNECT TO
!                      MEMORY with connective 1111 (Figure 20, p.76): a
!                      one at $2's bit, and $2 one bit on (p.21).
!   V+, $2, BIT        zero: $2 one bit on by the value field of
!                      "BIT VF, 0.1" (p.24).
!   CAB CB+, $1, LU    $1 one word on, count 64 down (p.43).
!
! THE DATA AND THE EXPECTED VALUES, worked by
! tests/verify_problem_4_matrix.py from the words as strap2 assembles them
! and the definition above, not by the model.  NUMB, 64 words in hex:
!   non-zero (12): words 0, 3, 7, 12, 18, 25, 31, 40, 47, 55, 62, 63 --
!   among them a fraction of 1 at exponent 48 (word 7), a negative
!   unnormalized fraction 1 with all three flags (word 12), exponents
!   -1000 and 1000, and, last, a negative word with flags T and V.
!   zero (52): zero words, and seven zero fractions that are not zero
!   words: exponent 5 (word 1), sign minus (2), flags only (4), exponent
!   -300 with sign and flags (9), exponent 1023 (20), exponent -1023 with
!   sign and a flag (33), and sign minus alone (50).
!   Expected:
!     BIMAGE         (16)9108204100810103
!     $1             value 64.0, count 0, refill XW1: (16)0010000000000026
!     $2             BIMAGE + 64 bits, count 0, refill XW2:
!                    (16)0032400000000027
!     location 7     the last CONNECT TO MEMORY stored one 1 bit: ones 1,
!                    left zeros 0 (p.76): (16)0000000000002000
!     word 8         word 63's bits 0-59, bits 60-63 still 0 (p.88)
!     word 9         0
!     word 10, $SB   sign 1, flags ZERO -- L, not LWF, sets the flag bits
!                    to zero (p.88): (16)0800000000000000
!     the guards and the halt at the printed BEW.
!
! PASSED AGAINST THE MODEL AS IT STOOD, 2026-11-16 (9 checks and the PC).
!
! INJECTION, DATA SIDE, OBSERVED 2026-11-16:
!   word 5 made non-zero, fraction 1 ("(16)0000000000000000  !5" ->
!   "(16)0000000000000010  !5", by --sub on the copy that runs; the
!   expected words are worked from the deck as it stands).  PREDICTED:
!   BIMAGE bit 5 alone; $2 steps one bit either way.  OBSERVED: FAIL BIMAGE
!   ((16)9508204100810103) and nothing else.
!
! --- printed p.37, Method 1 -------------------------------------------
START   LX, $1, XW1
        LX, $2, XW2
        Z, BIMAGE                       !'assume most are zeros
LU      L(U), NUMB($1)
        BZRZ, FIX                       !'usually unsuccessful
        V+, $2, BIT                     !'increase by one bit
CAB     CB+, $1, LU
        BEW, $
FIX     CM1111(BU, 1) (V+I), 0.1($2)
        B, CAB
BIT     VF, 0.1
XW1     XW, 0.0, 64, $
XW2     XW, BIMAGE, 0, $
! --- the deck's: the data, between guards; BIMAGE starts as all ones --
        SLC, 199.0
GUARD1  DD(BU,64),(16)A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5
BIMAGE  DD(BU,64),(16)FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF
NUMB    DD(BU,64),(16)0028000000000000  !0
        DD(BU,64),(16)00A0000000000000  !1
        DD(BU,64),(16)0000000000000008  !2
        DD(BU,64),(16)029ABCDEF0123458  !3
        DD(BU,64),(16)0000000000000007  !4
